    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/452064": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Biology Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $57,000.00 - $62,000.00 Salary/year Level Entry Position Type Full Time Apply Assistant Professor of Biology Illinois College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Biology with a focus on human health to begin August 2027. The ideal candidate will be committed to excellence in undergraduate education in the classroom and laboratory, and be enthusiastic about contributing to a ﬁrst-year science curriculum for biology, nursing, and health sciences majors.  Primary teaching duties include general biology and courses related to human health, which might include introductory microbiology, anatomy & physiology, and/or pathophysiology.  There are opportunities to develop new courses in the area of the candidate’s specialization.  The successful candidate will provide research opportunities for Illinois College undergraduates, as undergraduate research is a critical component of the mission of the Illinois College Biology Department. Doctorate (or ABD) in biology or a related ﬁeld. Illinois College seeks candidates who have a commitment to working closely with a wide range of students. Currently, our population is approximately one-quarter students of color and 40% first-generation college students. Eagerness and ability to work with these populations is essential. Equally important is excellence in pedagogy and an openness to student-centered teaching approaches. Founded by abolitionists, Illinois College was the first in Illinois to graduate students and hosts a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa. The College is student-focused, offering numerous opportunities for faculty-student interaction beyond the classroom, including collaborative research, international study-travel, and mentoring. Located in historic Jacksonville, Illinois—just 30 miles from Springfield and 70 miles from St. Louis—Illinois College has been transforming lives since 1829. Qualifications Applicants should submit the following materials in PDF format: Cover letter addressing teaching experience and interest in contributing to the mission of a student-focused institution. Curriculum Vitae. Contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. This position has a salary range of $57,000-$62,000 for the nine-month academic year with individual offers depending on field, experience, and education. Illinois College is an equal opportunity employer. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
