    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/452063": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Engineering You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Engineering Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $72,000.00 - $80,000.00 Salary/year Level Entry Position Type Full Time Apply Assistant Professor of Engineering Illinois College invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position in mechanical engineering to begin in fall 2027. This full-time faculty position requires a PhD or ABD in an engineering discipline. While we welcome candidates of a wide variety of expertise, preference will be given to those with skills or interest in teaching project-based undergraduate courses such as introductory engineering and capstone design, as well as lab-based courses such as materials science or fluid dynamics. Illinois College Engineering is a young program that has recently received ABET accreditation in mechanical engineering. The major is embedded within a liberal-arts college, and so understanding and appreciation of the environment of a liberal arts college is essential. Additional duties include contribution to the ongoing development of the engineering programs at the College, student advising and mentoring, and scholarly engagement. The successful candidate will be granted startup funds to help setup, including student-faculty research. This position resides within an interdisciplinary department including Physics, Mathematics, and Computer Science and hence presents an exciting opportunity for innovation and cross-disciplinary collaboration. Moreover, there are plentiful opportunities for meaningful engagement with our various local engineering partners. Illinois College seeks candidates who have a commitment to working closely with a wide range of students. Currently, our population is approximately one-quarter students of color and 40% first-generation college students. Eagerness and ability to work with these populations is essential. Equally important is excellence in pedagogy and an openness to student-centered teaching approaches. Founded by abolitionists, Illinois College was the first in Illinois to graduate students and hosts a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa. The College is student-focused, offering numerous opportunities for faculty-student interaction beyond the classroom, including collaborative research, international study-travel, and mentoring. Located in historic Jacksonville, Illinois—just 30 miles from Springfield and 70 miles from St. Louis—Illinois College has been transforming lives since 1829. Qualifications Applicants should submit the following materials in PDF format: Cover letter addressing teaching experience and interest in contributing to the mission of a student-focused institution. Curriculum Vitae. Contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. This position has a salary range of $72,000-$80,000 for the nine-month academic year with individual offers depending on field, experience, and education. Illinois College is an equal opportunity employer. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
