ravel, and mentoring. Located in historic Jacksonville, Illinois—just 30 miles from Springfield and 70 miles from St. Louis—Illinois College has been transforming lives since 1829. Qualifications Position Requirements: Master’s degree in Nursing (doctorate preferred) Unencumbered Illinois RN license in Illinois or the ability to get an Illinois RN license Minimum of two years clinical practice experience in the related specialty area Successful college teaching experience strongly preferred; enthusiasm for working toward pedagogical excellence required Intercultural competence and the ability to work with diverse populations Evidence of strong clinical skills and the ability to facilitate student learning in a clinical setting Applicants should submit the following materials in PDF format: Cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in undergraduate nursing education and interest in contributing to the mission of a student-focused institution. Curriculum Vitae. Contact information for three references. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. This position has a salary range of $64,000-$74,000 for the nine-month academic year with individual offers depending on field, experience, and education. Illinois College is an equal opportunity employer Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
