    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/445881": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (Nursing Department)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant (Nursing Department) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant (Nursing Department) Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $18.75 - $20.19 Hourly Position Type Full Time Job Shift Day Education Level Associate's Degree Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description The Administrative Assistant for the Nursing Program provides administrative support to the Director of the Nursing Program and to the program as a whole. Essential Functions: The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Assist the Director of Nursing with administrative tasks, including maintaining departmental documentation, organizing meetings, supporting communication with internal and external constituencies, and assisting with scheduling and planning. Serve as the first point of contact for the Nursing program, including for students, prospective students, IC personnel in other offices, and the public. Address or appropriately direct questions that arise from multiple constituencies, keeping the Director abreast of issues that arise. Support departmental efforts related to curriculum, assessment, accreditation, and quality improvement. Maintain departmental budget records, generate budget reports, and process requisitions and reimbursements for the Director and Nursing program faculty members. Participate in and prepare minutes for nursing program meetings. As needed, provide administrative support to Nursing Program faculty members. Qualifications Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree strongly preferred; equivalent education/experience considered Proficient with Microsoft Office; strong word processing data management abilities Ability to work effectively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written Experience with and understanding of accreditation and reporting processes and standards preferred Ability to deal with confidential information Capacity to take initiative where appropriate: a self-starter Interest in the Nursing profession; familiarity with health care professions preferred Excellent organizational and interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated ability to interact effectively with a wide range of internal and external constituencies Personal integrity and professionalism Highly organized, detail-oriented, with the ability to consistently multi-task Clear commitment to working in a higher education setting Additional Job Details: Job Title: Administrative Assistant for the Nursing Program Department: Nursing Reports to: Director of the Nursing Program Status: Hourly, 12-month, full-time About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/458074": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - CSEIB",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant - CSEIB You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant - CSEIB Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.00 - $21.50 Hourly Position Type Full Time Apply Description The Administrative Assistant provides administrative and operational support to the Director and professional staff and helps the Center for Student Engagement, Inclusion and Belonging maintain organized, accessible, and responsive services for students. The position serves as a welcoming first point of contact for students and campus partners and is responsible for administrative processes that allow the CSEIB to operate effectively. This individual also works closely with student leaders, student organizations, Greek Lettered Organizations (GLOs), and student employees. The position supports established processes and helps ensure that information, forms, calendars, records, and routine administrative work are accurate, timely, and accessible. Essential Functions The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Provide administrative support to the Director of Student Involvement and CSEIB professional staff, including maintaining budget documentation, organizing meetings, supporting communications, and assisting with scheduling and planning. Serve as a welcoming first point of contact for the CSEIB, including for students, student leaders, student organizations, GLOs, College employees, campus partners, and members of the public. Respond to routine questions and appropriately direct questions or concerns to the appropriate CSEIB staff member or campus office, keeping the Director and relevant staff informed of issues that arise. Maintain CSEIB records, shared files, forms, templates, procedures, calendars, and other administrative documentation to support accurate and efficient operations. Assist with routine administrative processes, including requisitions, reimbursements, purchasing documentation, equipment checkout, room or space reservations, tabling logistics, and related office needs. Support the CSEIB calendar and help ensure that meetings, events, deadlines, and student engagement opportunities are accurately represented and communicated. Provide administrative support for student organization and GLO processes, including maintaining rosters, officer information, required forms, registration materials, and other organization records. Assist with Presence, Jenzabar, and other software systems by entering or maintaining information, supporting forms and workflows, preparing reports, and helping ensure data accuracy and consistency. Maintain student engagement data and assessment processes by maintaining interaction records, organizing event and program information, and assisting with recurring reports and summaries. Assist with CSEIB programs, events, and initiatives, including event registration, logistics, materials, reservations, communications, attendance tracking, and post-event documentation. Coordinate with campus partners such as Information Technology, Institutional Research, Admissions, Residential Life, Student Success, Campus Services, Accounting, and other offices as appropriate. Perform other duties and responsibilities consistent with the position and assigned by the Director. Qualifications Qualifications: Associate’s degree required; bachelor’s degree strongly preferred. Equivalent education and relevant experience may be considered. Relevant administrative experience, preferably in higher education. Proficiency with Microsoft Office; comfort learning institutional technology and administrative systems. Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community members from a wide range of backgrounds and experiences. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion, sound judgment, and professionalism. Ability to take initiative, solve routine problems, follow established processes, and identify opportunities for practical improvement. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively as part of a team and independently when appropriate. Commitment to providing welcoming, student-centered service in a higher education environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with students in a college or university administrative or student services environment. Experience with student information systems, event-management platforms, engagement platforms, or comparable technology. Experience with data entry, reporting, assessment, or dashboard-related work. Experience coordinating events, meetings, calendars, and/or administrative projects. Additional Job Details Job Title: Administrative Assistant for the Center for Student Engagement, Inclusion and Belonging (CSEIB) Department: Center for Student Engagement, Inclusion and Belonging Reports To: Director of Student Involvement and the Center for Student Engagement, Inclusion and Belonging Status: Hourly, 10-month, full-time Date Last Revised: October 2026 About Illinois College Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students’ qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/447548": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Admission Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admission Counselor Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $43,000.00 - $46,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Degree Travel Percentage Up to 25% Apply Description Description Become a recruiter, marketer, advisor, storyteller, presenter, and relationship builder…all in one role. Build relationships, solve problems, and help students make life-changing decisions while developing skills that will serve you throughout your career. If you're energized by connecting with people, thrive in a fast-paced environment, and want a career where no two days are the same, we'd love to meet you. As an Admission Counselor, you'll work with high school students and families, delivering presentations, executing events, analyzing data, and helping prospective students navigate one of the most important decisions of their lives. You'll travel throughout your assigned territory, represent Illinois College at schools and community events, review applications, and partner with colleagues to achieve shared enrollment goals.  Along the way, you'll gain real-world experience in consultative sales, marketing, public speaking, project management, and strategic decision-making. Essential Functions: The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Counsel prospective students and their families as they seek to learn about the value of an Illinois College education. Act as Territory Manager for an assigned region within the US to realize an assigned recruitment goal. Meet weekly goals for counselor initiated completed contacts. Respond to in-person, phone and electronic admissions inquiries in a timely manner and at times that are appropriate for different time zones. Review applications for admission and scholarships Assist with on-campus, off-campus, and virtual recruiting events and conduct information sessions. Conduct follow-up with prospective students at times that are convenient for different domestic time zones Provide enlightened hospitality to create lasting connections with prospective students, families and school counseling staff. Work with others to support division-wide enrollment initiatives such as event planning, program management, communication flow, and other duties as assigned. Qualifications Qualifications: Bachelors degree, required This position includes seasonal travel within an assigned territory, along with occasional evening and weekend recruitment events planned in advance Dynamic public speaker with excellent writing and interpersonal skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively as a goal-oriented strategic thinker Intercultural competence and the ability to work with diverse populations Must have a valid driver’s license and evidence of insurability Must be able to lift and carry 30 pounds, reach above shoulders, bend at the waist, stand for extended periods of time. Additional Job Details: Job Title: Admission Counselor Department: Office of Admission Reports to: Director of Recruitment and Outreach Status : Full Time, Salary Date Last Revised: July 2026 Salary Range: $43,000 - $46,000 Travel Percentage up to 25% Benefits Information: To view benefit information related to this position, please visit this link . About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
