    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/455981": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Director of Admission",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Director of Admission You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Director of Admission Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $46,000.00 - $55,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Degree Travel Percentage Up to 25% Apply Description The Assistant/Associate Director of Admission plays a leadership role in developing and implementing programs and activities designed to enroll new undergraduate students at Illinois College (IC). As a member of the Enrollment team, the assistant/associate director participates in a full range of recruitment and admission efforts including recruitment travel, group presentations, individual meetings, financial aid counseling, application review. Additionally, this position will take the lead on various admission strategy initiatives aligned to the strengths and interests of the successful candidate. Essential Functions: The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Counsel prospective students and their families as they seek to learn about the value of an Illinois College education. Act as Territory Manager for an assigned region within the US to realize an assigned recruitment goal. Meet weekly goals for counselor-initiated completed contacts. Respond to in-person, phone, and electronic admissions inquiries in a timely manner and at times that are appropriate for different time zones. Review applications for admission and scholarships. Assist with on- and off-campus recruiting events and conduct information sessions. Conduct follow-up with prospective students at times that are convenient for different domestic time zones Provide enlightened hospitality to create lasting connections with prospective students, families and school counseling staff. Take the lead on one or more projects supporting enrollment success, such as communication strategy, data analysis, social media, etc. Engage in College-wide initiatives to support student success, achieve strategic growth and build sustainable foundations. Qualifications Qualifications: Ability to develop and maintain collaborative working relationships, engage in creative problem-solving and extend enlightened hospitality when working with others Intermediate knowledge of Slate CRM, Microsoft Office, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and the Google suite of office products. Two to five years of experience in admission and/or financial aid with progressive responsibility and measurable success. Experience level will determine final position title Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively Intercultural competency; ability to work well with individuals of diverse background Bachelor’s degree required Must be able to lift and carry 30 pounds, reach above shoulders, bend at the waist, stand for extended periods of time. Additional Job Details: Job Title: Assistant/Associate Director of Admission Department: Office of Admission Reports to: Director of Recruitment and Outreach Status: Full-time, Salaried, 12-month Date Last Revised: September 2026 About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
