    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/453253": {
      "title": "Enrollment Specialist  (Online Students)",
      "description": "Enrollment Specialist  (Online Students) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Enrollment Specialist  (Online Students) Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $44,000.00 - $48,000.00 Salary/year Level Entry Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Degree Travel Percentage Up to 25% Apply Description If you want a job where the impact of your work is visible every week with real students, real decisions and real results, join the team as an Enrollment Specialist for Online Students. Illinois College is growing its online undergraduate programs fast — and we're looking for a recruiter who's ready to grow with it. If you're early in your career and looking for a role that builds real sales, marketing, and relationship-building skills inside a mission-driven environment, this is a great place to start. You’ll work with a pipeline of prospective students to help them figure out if Illinois College is the right next step, with opportunities for building relationships by phone, email and text. We’re looking for someone organized and curious who enjoys clear goals and the satisfaction of hitting them. You’ll also get a chance to work with individuals all over the globe, helping bring ambitious students from around the world to our Jacksonville, Illinois campus. Meet enrollment and goals to help the College realize online enrollment growth while helping people make life-changing decisions about their education. Manage relationships with strong communication skills and follow through. Meet weekly goals for counselor-initiated contacts and other key recruitment activities. Review applications for admission and scholarships using sound, program-appropriate judgment. Respond to in-person, phone, and electronic admissions inquiries in a timely manner and at times that are appropriate for different time zones (domestic and international). Maintain accurate, up-to-date records of prospective student communications and activity in the CRM. Collaborate with Financial Aid, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to remove barriers and support students from inquiry to enrollment. Support a smaller portfolio of international undergraduate recruitment, helping prospective students navigate admission and, where applicable, visa-related requirements. Represent Illinois College at occasional recruiting events, fairs, and info sessions, including some evening, weekend, and travel commitments during peak season. Qualifications What You'll Bring A bachelor's degree Prior sales, customer service, or admissions experience, preferred Genuine interest in people; asking good questions and listening to the answers Comfort picking up the phone and having conversations, even with people you've never met A goal-oriented mindset; knowing what you're working toward and tracking your progress Exposure to CRM/database tools like Slate, preferred Sharp writing and communication skills Comfort working independently while staying connected to a team Flexibility to work some evenings/weekends during peak season, and travel occasionally (including internationally) Additional Job Details: Job Title: Enrollment Specialist (Online) Department: Admission Reports to: Director of Specialized Admission Initiatives Status : Full Time, 12 month, Salary Date Last Revised: September 2026 Pay Information: $44,000 - $48,000 Benefits Information: To view benefit information related to this position, please visit https://www.ic.edu/humanresources/benefits About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/444805": {
      "title": "Head Coach Swim",
      "description": "Head Coach Swim You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Coach Swim Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $45,000.00 - $55,000.00 Salary/year Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Apply Description The primary function of the Head Swim Coach is to facilitate all operations of successful men’s and women’s swim programs, including recruiting, retaining and coaching members of the swim team.  The Head Swim Coach is responsible for day-to-day coaching responsibilities and is expected to meet annual recruiting and retention goals.  The head coach is responsible for facilitating the coordination of travel, competition management, equipment management, camps, and fundraising. In addition to the day-to-day duties of coaching the swim programs, this position serves as the pool manager and provides daily management, maintenance, and routine cleaning of the natatorium. Essential Functions The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Coaching 80% Recruit, retain and graduate successful student-athletes In direct planning with the Director of Athletics and the office of admissions, develop and execute recruiting strategies to meet the recruitment and retention goals set by the College Ensure academic performance and personal development of student-athletes by engaging with the Core Retention Group and the Student Life team Coordinate all aspects of a successful swim program including scheduling and facilitating competition, daily practice plans, player management, equipment management, camps, and fundraising Demonstrate high level of intercultural competence and the ability to work with diverse population Maintain a high level of professionalism on and off the pool deck toward student athletes, other coaches, parents, administrators, and members of the community Adhere to all Illinois College, Midwest Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations Attend regular athletic and admission staff meetings Assume additional administrative responsibilities within Athletics Department, as assigned by the Director of Athletics Pool Management 20% Monitor chemical balance for the swimming pool and hot tub, daily; adjusting levels, as needed Check mechanical operations, daily Operate robotic pool cleaner and clean the filter bags twice a week Backwash the pool and hot tub every two weeks Shock the pool and hot tub, monthly Order all chemicals for pool operations, as needed Report all mechanical and electrical problems to Facilities Management Hire and supervise student workers and lifeguards Annually meet and discuss pool operation with the State Inspector Qualifications Qualifications Bachelor’s degree, required Intercultural competency; ability to work with individuals of diverse backgrounds Able to develop and maintain collaborative relationships, engage in creative problem-solving, and extend enlightened hospitality when working with others. Valid driver’s license and evidence of insurability, required Swim coaching experience at the NCAA level, Division III, preferred Recruiting experience at the collegiate level, Division III, preferred Must understand and value the liberal arts experience for students at Illinois College, especially including participation in other sports, clubs and organizations, and having an academic experience Ability to obtain an Illinois Department of Health Pool Operator Certification First Aid and AED certification, preferred Ability to work weekdays, weekends, and some evenings Strong oral and written communication skills Possess an outcomes-oriented approach to coaching Ability to lift 30 pounds Job Title: Head Men’s and Women’s Swim Coach/Pool Manager Department: Athletics Reports to: Assistant AD Status: Full Time, Salaried Exempt (12-month) Date Last Revised: August 2026 About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/450751": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Maintenance Technician Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $18.00 - $18.00 Hourly Level Experienced Apply Description The Maintenance Technician performs supervised routine maintenance tasks, following specific detailed instructions in the maintenance of campus buildings and grounds. This individual is a self-motivated team player who works effectively with technical and non-technical team members and outside individuals. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Assists with maintaining HVAC equipment (e.g. changes filters) Processes daily work orders Has ability to perform miscellaneous electrical, plumbing, and carpentry tasks Assists with repairs system controllers, wiring, and functions Assists when needed with reading and checking gauges, meters, and thermometers and records readings on log sheets Checks operation of equipment and reports to supervisor needed repairs for buildings and mechanical equipment Operates necessary equipment to perform the job (e.g. driving Kubotas, forklift, snow removal equipment and various power tools) Assists with the responsibility for securing an inventory of supplies and equipment Maintains operating records as required Assists with campus event setups Supervises and trains subordinates and other assigned personnel as required Responds to emergencies in off-hours, as necessary. Rotating on-call shifts posted weekly. Has knowledge of and operates within OSHA standards and college safety policies at all times Qualifications Qualifications: High school or equivalent, required Demonstrable work history reflecting reliability and dependability Must possess a current drivers license and evidence of insurability Intercultural competency, ability to work well with people of diverse backgrounds Ability to work from stepladders with or without accommodations Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide units of measure Ability to follow written and verbal instructions and perform duties with minimal supervision Ability to stoop, bend, stand, walk, reach, kneel, climb, or balance frequently and for extended periods of time while performing job duties Good verbal and written communication skills Excellent customer service skills are required Two years of building maintenance experience, preferred Must possess sufficient strength and stamina to lift and carry equipment weighing up to 75 lbs. Additional Job Details: Job Title: Maintenance Technician Department: Facilities Management Reports to: Maintenance Supervisor Status: Full Time, Hourly $18.00 per hour Class: Non-exempt Date Last Revised: August 2026 Tuesday-Saturday 8:00a.m-4:30p.m About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/449670": {
      "title": "Payroll Coordinator",
      "description": "Payroll Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Payroll Coordinator Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.70 - $25.42 Hourly Level Entry Position Type Full Time Education Level Associate's Degree Apply Description Summary The Payroll Coordinator is responsible for the accurate and timely administration of all College payrolls. The Payroll Coordinator will be expected to work in a fast-paced setting and provide service as the primary resource for students, faculty, and supervisors regarding payroll-related questions. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Payroll Coordinator Process biweekly/semi-monthly/monthly payrolls accurately and timely, including regular wages, overtime, stipends, deductions, and other earnings Administer the employment side of the Federal Work Study (FWS) program, to include: Assign Federal Work Study semester maximums for each eligible student in the payroll system Monitor utilization of student FWS each pay period Transition students to regular work upon reaching their FWS maximum Create periodic FWS utilization reports for Student Financial Services Complete annual FWS audit Monitor and address the students exceeding the 10 hour/week maximum Reconcile insurance statements to employee deductions and general ledger liability accounts on a monthly basis; timely identify and resolve any discrepancies. Submit requisitions for insurance vendor payments and payroll deduction payments (i.e. PLUW) Annually review W2 and 1095 reports from payroll system Assist with audits and provide payroll documentation and reports, as requested Maintain accurate and confidential payroll records and employee payroll information Maintain payroll related items on HRIS. Develop and maintain current desk procedures. Stay abreast of the latest changes to payroll laws, regulations, and tax requirements. Job Title: Payroll Coordinator Department: Human Resources Reports to: Director of Human Resources Status: Full-time, $20.70-$25.42 per hour. Class: Non-Exempt Date Last Revised: August 2026 Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in historic Jacksonville, Illinois, 85 miles north of St. Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the Illinois State Capital. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. Illinois College promotes academic freedom, equality of opportunity, and human dignity through an increasingly diverse student population. The College develops in its student’s qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Qualifications Qualifications Associate’s degree in accounting, finance, business administration, human resources, or related field, required . Three years of comparable work experience may be substituted in place of this degree requirement Minimum 2 years’ experience in payroll administration, strongly preferred Strong knowledge of payroll processing, timekeeping, wage and hour requirements, and payroll deductions Strong computer skills, specifically experience working with Microsoft Excel and HRIS systems High attention to detail Ability to handle sensitive information and maintain confidentiality Excellent written and oral communication skills Strong organizational skills Ability to multi-task and effectively prioritize tasks Ability to identify and implement efficient workflows Possess tact and have a friendly demeanor Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A1F01429B0D77840F84E7C37F0997E7/jobs/459259": {
      "title": "Major Gift Officer",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Major Gift Officer Illinois College - Jacksonville, IL 62650 Apply Overview Salary Range $75,000.00 - $90,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description The fundamental mission of Illinois College’s Office of Development and Alumni Engagement is to fulfill the inherent need for external support. Major Gift Officers are responsible for the identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift donors at the $25,000+ level. They provide strategic assistance to the fundraising team, which includes the President, and Vice President of External Relations, to meet the College’s fundraising goals. This is a location flexible position within a few hours’ drive of the Jacksonville, Illinois campus. Essential Functions: The following list of duties is meant to be representative of the work performed in this position. The omission of a specific duty or responsibility will not preclude it from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical extension of position responsibilities. Meet or exceed fundraising goals through the management of a portfolio of up to 150 major and planned gift donors and prospects. Solicit major gifts through meetings via face-to-face, telephone, or virtual appointments, as well as personalized mailings, in order to obtain first-time and increased major donor contributions. Conduct at least 15 face-to-face visits with donors and prospects per month (travel required). Serve as a key member of the fundraising team and actively participate in developing strategies to achieve institutional goals for student success, strategic growth, and sustainable foundations. Work closely with senior leaders, faculty, staff, and volunteers to guide the identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major donor relationships. Collaborate with the Assistant Vice President of Advancement to prepare major and planned giving proposals, illustrations of life income and estate gift arrangements and gift agreements. Work closely with the Director of Annual Programs and Advancement Communication to increase awareness of major, planned, and leadership annual gifts through press releases and feature stories in the Quarterly magazine, the College website, social media, and print publications. Qualifications Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and at least five years of applicable experience, required. Relationship-building experience in higher education and/or non-profit organizations. A strong appreciation for the value of private, liberal-arts-based education is a fundamental attribute. Intercultural competency; ability to work well with individuals of diverse backgrounds. Ability to communicate effectively, orally and in writing, work independently and within a team, handle confidential information with utmost discretion, and navigate sensitive situations. Able to develop and maintain collaborative relationships, engage in creative problem-solving, and extend enlightened hospitality when working with others. Must be comfortable working in an environment where fundraising metrics play an essential role in annual performance evaluations. Experience with or willingness to learn office software programs such as Word and Excel, Microsoft Teams or Google Docs and constituent relations software, such as Raiser's Edge NXT. Overnight travel as well as evenings and weekend work required with advanced notice. Must have a valid drivers license and a good driving record. Additional Job Details: Job Title: Major Gift Officer Department: Office of Development and Alumni Relations Reports to: Assistant Vice President of Advancement Status: Full Time, Salaried Class: Administrative Exemption Date Last Revised: September 2022 About Illinois College: Illinois College is a residential, private liberal arts college located in the heart of Illinois, 70 miles northeast of Saint Louis, Missouri, and 30 miles west of Springfield, the capital of Illinois. True to its founding vision in 1829, Illinois College is a community committed to the highest standards of scholarship and integrity in the liberal arts. The College develops in its students qualities of mind and character needed for fulfilling lives of leadership and service, fostering academic excellence rooted in opportunities for experiential learning while preparing students for lifelong success. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
